Z||000000||lildevil||08-14-2001||10:07 PM||||What is the widest tire that will fit the rear of my 85 Fiero on 17 inch wheels. I am thinkin 245 45 17's. Anyone have them. Also how much will the 17's slow my car down in the 1/4?<P><P>------------------<BR>Earl Sessions<BR>1985 Fiero w/ 1998 Supercharged 3.8 V-6<BR>Best ET: 13.311 @100.75 mph<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||KRMFiero||08-14-2001||10:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lildevil:<BR><B>What is the widest tire that will fit the rear of my 85 Fiero on 17 inch wheels. I am thinkin 245 45 17's. Anyone have them. Also how much will the 17's slow my car down in the 1/4?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Lets see, widest tire i belive is 245/45.... Buy me a set  of 17's and ill tell you how much they slow me down  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||AkursedX||08-15-2001||12:42 AM||||It depends on the width of your rim.  I run 17x8 rims in the rear with 235/45/17's.  They fit easily.  I would go with 245/40/17's, I think those would be the widest, and I think the 45 series are too tall at that width, but that's just my opinion.  But with 8 inch rims, you might even be able to run 255/40/17's in the rear, but I'm not 100% sure on that.<P>As far as the rims hurting your acceleration, that depends mostly on the wieght of your tire/rim setup.  My tires in total weigh 27lbs more than the stock setup, so my acceleration is probably effected somewhat.  I don't think it's alot though.  But if you have lighter ries and rims (you could probably find a tire/rim setup that would cut 30lbs from the total weight (i.e. SSR Competition's) than you would probably get some better acceleration.<P>Hope this helps  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||08-15-2001||01:05 AM||||My car gained some speed in the 1/4, even though the new wheels/tyres are a bit heavier.<P>It was because the Tyres grip much better than the crappy 15" tyres I had before.<P>Go for it, fieros love 17" wheels.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.||||reg||3
